load("//translator/build_defs:convert_cmake_project.bzl", "convert_autotools_project")

# Fourth Autotools corpus project. Selection rationale is in the
# `libmicrohttpd` http_archive comment in MODULE.bazel; the short version is
# that it validates the automake TESTS classifier's MAJORITY branch, which
# jansson — the project that motivated the classifier — structurally cannot
# reach.
#
#   TESTS = $(check_PROGRAMS)   <- libmicrohttpd, and most projects
#   a shell script              <- jansson, xz
#
# Also the largest Autotools project in the corpus at 118 own .c files, which
# is the point: jansson at 14 made a bug obvious, this one checks the fix
# holds at scale.
#
# Sources come from the @libmicrohttpd http_archive (pinned in MODULE.bazel)
# as a release TARBALL. source_dir is left empty so the rule derives it from
# where configure.ac landed.
#
# Green post-agent: 111 targets, 94 expressed tests, 16 ground-truth
# comparisons and 30 module tests pass. The classifier's majority branch is
# validated — 94 tests came from `TESTS = $(check_PROGRAMS)`, the shape
# jansson could not reach.
#
# Three translator gaps found and fixed, all from scale rather than novelty:
#
#  - `$(am__EXEEXT_N)` needed TRANSITIVE expansion; one level left 14 tests
#    escalating as literal variable text.
#  - The same variables are declared per directory (five times for
#    `am__EXEEXT_1`, one of them empty), so they must accumulate like
#    primaries. Last-wins lost four definitions.
#  - A source that is BOTH `#include`d and compiled must stay in srcs. The
#    textual-include detection from expat assumed the roles are exclusive,
#    and test_postprocessor_md lost three sources to it (bzl-e31).
#
# 65 test targets are currently not expressed, and the reason first recorded
# here was WRONG. It said libcurl is "a third-party library the conversion
# cannot supply". libcurl is installed on this machine — at the multiarch
# path `/usr/include/x86_64-linux-gnu/curl/` — and the project's own `make
# check` compiles and links all 65 against it.
#
# The real gap is that this is the corpus's FIRST project depending on a
# library it does not itself build, and the pipeline has no path for that
# (bzl-x8l). `external_links` is collected and then discarded, so the
# dependency vanishes with no escalation.
#
# The fix is NOT to emit `-lcurl`: linking a host library would break the
# hermeticity CLAUDE.md requires of generated output. The dependency has to
# be CONVERTED and depended on as another Bazel module, which is what the
# validation workspace's cross-module `bazel_dep` wiring already exists to
# support. Until then these 65 are an open gap, not a resolved omission —
# and this project's post-agent green was reached by deleting them, which
# the gate could not distinguish from a real pass (bzl-ned).
#
# HTTPS is a different and legitimate case: disabled rather than
# host-captured, since the module ships no GnuTLS and automake puts
# connection_https.c behind `if ENABLE_HTTPS`.
convert_autotools_project(
    name = "converted",
    srcs = ["@libmicrohttpd//:all_srcs"],
    visibility = ["//translator/tests:__pkg__"],
)
